    <!-- Unit Overview -->
    <section class="welcome-section">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-compass section-icon"></i> Unit Overview</h2>
        <p>of Computer Science Unit Foundation Concepts The focus is on Architectural Abstraction and Proactive Defense. While SL covers the "what" of networks, HL investigates the "how"—specifically the orchestration of the TCP/IP Stack, the logic of Dynamic Routing, and the implementation of active countermeasures like IDS/IPS.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Syllabus Links -->
    <section class="content-section">
        <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-bookmark section-icon"></i> What You'll Learn</h2>
        <div class="learning-points">
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>A2.1.5</strong> — The TCP/IP Model: Deep dive into the four layers (Application, Transport, Network, Data Link/Physical). Concepts of Encapsulation and Protocol Data Units (PDUs).
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>A2.2.2</strong> — Advanced Server Types: Reverse Proxy (load balancing/security), Proxy Servers (anonymity/caching), and specialised Database/Web servers.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>A2.3.4</strong> — Dynamic Routing: Mechanics of routing tables, discovery protocols, and how routers determine the "optimal path" across complex, shifting networks.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>A2.4.2</strong> — -3: Network Countermeasures: Differentiating between Intrusion Detection Systems (IDS) and Intrusion Prevention Systems (IPS). Identifying and mitigating sophisticated network threats.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

